# Concept Layer — Era Implementation Status

A per-era rollup across the 45-version roadmap (`00-architecture.docs`), in the same format
as `beaver-desktop/features/gui/infra/eras_implementation.docs` (this roadmap's requested
versioning reference). This is a summary/index, not a replacement for the per-era `.docs`
files (each version carries its own Goal / Reuses / Implement / Validate / Done-when) or
`gaps/00-index.docs`.

Legend: ✅ done · 🟡 in progress · ⬜ not started · ⚠️ partial · ⛔ blocked on a missing
dependency

**Overall: ✅ All four phases done, verified 2026-09-17 · quality-revised 2026-09-17 ·
admin removed 2026-09-17 (gap 2 in `gaps/00-index.docs`; sibling roadmap's `gaps/013`). **29**
concept pages published under `/concepts/` (`concepts/administrative-commands.mdx` deleted by
explicit user instruction — every "30 pages" mention below this line predates that removal
and is a historical record, not current fact), reachable from a new "Concepts" group in the
Guides tab (second position, after Getting started); 3 existing pages extended for the merge
topics (`choose-your-setup.mdx`, `installation.mdx`, `connect.mdx`); 4 task guides and 36
`cli/*.mdx` reference pages gained a link back to their paired concept page. **Post-launch
quality pass (gap 010):** direct user feedback that the pages read as flat and reference-like
led to studying Vercel's and Conductor's concept-page style (fetched live via `WebFetch`,
not assumed) and rewriting all 30 pages to match — bolded-term lead definitions, verified
real command snippets, targeted comparison tables, narrative section headings. Caught and
fixed 4 inaccurate command examples in the process by verifying each against its source
`cli/*.mdx` page before publishing. Template and worked example updated to match; the worked
example is now a live copy of the real `concepts/services.mdx`. Full disclosure sweep and
`mint broken-links` clean throughout, both before and after the rewrite.**

Repo: `mintlify` (`main`). No backend or CLI changes required at any point — this roadmap
produces documentation content only.

---

## Relationship to `/features/docs/` (CLI Documentation Closure)

| Their era | Status (per their own `00-architecture.docs`) | Use here |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Era 1 — command inventory | not tracked as done here; check their file at execution time | Era 1 here cross-references existing pages, not their command inventory directly, but Eras 3–11 here link to whatever their Eras 3–11 eventually produce |
| Era 2 — templates & disclosure | — | `DISCLOSURE.md` and the fictional vocabulary reused wholesale by this roadmap's Era 2 |
| Eras 3–11 — family reference pages | — | Every concept page's "command reference" link target; not blocking, but a concept page linking to an unwritten reference page must say so honestly (per their own Invariant 9 pattern) |
| Era 12 — task guides & CLI nav | — | The four existing task guides are this roadmap's direct link-back targets (Era 12 V41 here) |
| Era 13 — verification & sustaining | — | This roadmap's Era 13 V45 extends their `CLAUDE.md` sustaining section rather than duplicating it |

**Sequencing note.** This roadmap's Phase 1 (Eras 1–2) can start immediately — it does not
wait on the sibling roadmap. Phase 2 family eras here can also start immediately per topic;
only each page's final reference-link target may need a placeholder note until the sibling
roadmap's matching family lands. Era 12 (nav + bidirectional linking) is easiest run once
the sibling roadmap's Phase 2 is well underway, but is not formally gated on it finishing.

---

## Phase 1 — Foundation (reuse, don't rebuild)

### Era 1 — Inventory & Placement (V1–V3) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

Topic checklist transcription, cross-reference against existing pages, nav-home decision.
`inventory/00-topics.docs` (34/34 topics, verbatim from `concepts-explained.txt`) and
`inventory/01-cross-reference.docs` (every topic classified against the actual current file
tree and the now-accurate `/features/docs/inventory/doc_status.csv`) written and checked.
Result: **4 merge-into-existing candidates** (T2 `choose-your-setup.mdx`, T3
`installation.mdx`, T6 `connect.mdx`+`machine-roles.mdx`, T11
`deploying/environment-variables.mdx`, each with a named gap, not a blanket "already done"),
**28 new-page candidates**, **1 classify-first** (T34, deferred to Era 11 by design). One
naming collision caught and resolved: T25 (Firewall, Beaver's own product feature) is
explicitly distinguished from the similarly-named but unrelated
`infrastructure-setup/firewall-requirements.mdx` (OS/cloud-provider port configuration) so
Era 7 doesn't conflate or duplicate them.

### Era 2 — Template & Disclosure (V4–V5) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

Concept page template + filled example (Services); `DISCLOSURE-ADDENDUM.md` extending the
sibling roadmap's `DISCLOSURE.md`. Both drafted during planning, **re-verified this pass**:
one real bug found and fixed — the template's original `{{placeholder}}` syntax is invalid
MDX and was breaking `mint broken-links` for the entire site (not just this file), fixed by
switching to `[[placeholder]]`. `mint broken-links` now clean site-wide. The addendum's
two-pass-topics list cross-checked against Era 1's final classification: complete.

