## Cross-cutting risk register

| Risk | Era | Mitigation designed in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Concept pages drift into reference-page territory (flag tables, exhaustive syntax) | all Phase 2 | Invariant 1 (concept altitude); template has no flag-table section at all |
| Two roadmaps' reference-page edits collide | 12 | V41 explicitly checks the sibling roadmap's own status before editing shared `cli/*.mdx` files |
| Concept page links to a reference page that doesn't exist yet | 3–11 | Honest placeholder notes, resolved at Era 12 V41, same pattern the sibling roadmap already uses for its own cross-links |
| Disclosure leak at concept altitude (higher risk than command altitude) | all Phase 2, esp. 5/7/10/11 | `DISCLOSURE-ADDENDUM.md`; two-pass topics named explicitly; Era 13 V44 full sweep |
| Duplicated content between new Concepts group and existing Getting-Started pages | 3, 4, 5 | Invariant 9; Era 1 V2 classification is binding, deviations logged not silently made |
| Destructive-action claims (Persistent storage, Rollback) stated incorrectly | 9, 10 | Invariant 1 applied with elevated stakes — explicitly called out as highest-accuracy requirement |
| Nav position doesn't actually improve discoverability | 12 | Era 1 V3's placement reasoning recorded with rejected alternatives, so it's a decision, not a guess, and revisitable if wrong |

---

## Naming decisions

- **The roadmap folder is `features/concepts/`** inside `mintlify`, restarting its own
  V-line (V1–V45), exactly as `features/docs/` restarts its own and as
  `beaver-desktop/features/gui/infra/` restarts its own relative to `features/gui/`.
- **Published pages live under a new top-level `concepts/` directory**, mirroring the
  existing `guides/` directory pattern — not nested under `cli/` (the explicit instruction
  this roadmap exists to satisfy) and not merged into `guides/` (concepts and task guides
  are different altitudes, kept as visibly different nav groups).
- **"Concepts" is the nav group name**, matching the term `concepts-explained.txt` itself
  uses throughout, so the sidebar label matches the vocabulary already established in the
  planning conversation this roadmap is built from.
- **This roadmap does not supersede or restructure `/features/docs/`** — the two are peers,
  cross-referenced throughout, each owning a distinct layer (concept vs. reference) of the
  same three-layer model.
